From u7a370588160d954e at groups.google.com  Wed Sep 12 16:06:10 2012
From: u7a370588160d954e at groups.google.com (Natalie Asselin)
Date: Wed, 12 Sep 2012 16:06:10 +0000
Subject: Re: DSM error message
Message-ID: <rveFstk6ujY.O7gOsvnmRPYJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <rveFstk6ujY.EGgyDSNKbrgJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
References: <rveFstk6ujY.EGgyDSNKbrgJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/rveFstk6ujY/m/O7gOsvnmRPYJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RESOLVED

Hello list,

Turns out my 'Error message' was caused by the Object column in my Observ=
ation data layer having been imported as 'Text' instead of 'Integer'. Onc=
e I re-imported the data and corrected this mistake, the analysis ran wit=
hout error.

To note: the MRDS and CDS analyses had run without errors which lead to m=
e assume I had correctly imported the data. But this was not the case.=20=

Many thanks to all that replied to my message.=20

Natalie.

